{"agent":"fleet-forecastcycle","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The guard is narrowed to open items (`chain_cycles` builds `open_items = {k: v for k, v in live.items() if v.state != DONE}` and drops every edge whose target is not in `open_items`), but the longest-chain walk still runs over `items` from `_chain_scope`, which returns the same `live` mapping unfiltered. The very existence of the `v.state != DONE` filter is the proof that `live` contains finished items — otherwise the filter would be dead code. Before this change the guard and the walk used exactly the same node set (`find_cycles(items, edges=before)`), so the walk could never be handed a cyclic graph. Now it can.\n\nConcrete input: task A (open) whose `needs` is [B], task B (done) whose needs is [C], task C (done) whose needs is [B]. `chain_cycles(state, \"\")` filters to `open_items == {A}`, sees no edge out of A, and returns `[]`, so `critical_path` proceeds to the walk over `items == {A, B, C}` — a graph that is cyclic (B↔C). The `seen` set stops the recursion, but the memo is populated from a search restricted by `seen`, so values computed for one start are reused where they are invalid: this is precisely the \"confidently wrong number\" the removed guard's own comment says it refuses (\"The longest chain is only defined on an acyclic graph: on a cyclic one a chain computed for one node is reused where it is wrong\"). Even in the acyclic case A(open)→B(done), the returned chain is [A, B] although the docstring promises the chain \"among not-done items\" and only A remains to run, so the forecast figure is inflated. Cycles through finished items are reachable via `cycle_policy = \"warn\"`, which the same comment cites as the reason the guard exists. The regression test only asserts that *a* figure is returned, so it passes while the number is wrong; the walk (or `items`) must be restricted to the open items, matching `chain_cycles`, for the guard to protect what is actually traversed.","digest":"3212496bcca44a06","location":"ddflow/core/schedule.py — `critical_path` cycle guard vs. the node set it walks","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/core/schedule.py — `critical_path` cycle guard vs. the node set it walks"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":8191,"diff_sha":"67e82ed60fd59289812f105672fce7fec80d3054d91834ee12811cea1a00dd26","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":484.9,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"143337d92751dc79","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Bbbcbfc4bbb.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261015T205918Z-274c59f0.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"ef266634f825fcaccfac2e9a1710a6ea04231b29","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/core/schedule.py — `critical_path` cycle guard vs. the node set it walks"],"tree_sha":"ef266634f825+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"ebc6234fa7a1fcc917a22e7e1","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":65356,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-Bbbcbfc4bbb","ts":"2026-10-15T21:07:24.133358Z"}
